    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Farmstead planning</span> is the deliberate arrangement of farm buildings and structures (barns, silos, poultry houses, fish ponds, stores) on a farm to promote efficiency, convenience and safety.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Farmstead Planning</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Farmstead planning refers to deciding the best location and layout of all buildings and structures used for farm operations, so that movement of people, animals, equipment and produce is efficient and costs are minimised.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Factors Affecting Location of Farm Buildings/Structures</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Topography</td><td>Flat, well-drained land is preferred to avoid flooding and ease construction</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Soil type</td><td>Firm, well-drained soils give a stable foundation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Water supply</td><td>Structures like poultry houses and fish ponds need reliable, nearby water</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Nearness to market</td><td>Reduces transport cost and time to sell produce</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Accessibility</td><td>Good roads ease movement of inputs, produce and labour</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Wind direction</td><td>Poultry/piggery sited downwind of the farmhouse to reduce odour</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Security</td><td>Structures sited where they can be easily monitored/protected</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Layout of Common Farm Structures</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Barns</strong> are usually sited close to the field/farmhouse for easy storage of produce and implements. <strong>Silos</strong> are placed near feeding areas for convenience in moving stored feed to livestock. <strong>Poultry houses</strong> are sited on well-drained, elevated ground away from the farmhouse (for hygiene) but accessible by road. <strong>Fish ponds</strong> require a reliable water source and are sited on gently sloping land to allow easy filling and draining.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Importance of Good Farmstead Planning</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A well-planned farmstead reduces the time and labour needed to move between structures, minimises the spread of pests and diseases, improves safety and hygiene, protects structures from flooding, and increases overall efficiency and productivity of the farm.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC frequently asks why poultry houses should not be built too close to the farmhouse — the answer centres on hygiene, disease control and odour, not distance to market.\n</div>\n',
