    term: 'First Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Ornamental plants</span> are plants grown mainly for their beauty and decorative value rather than for food. They play important economic, aesthetic, medicinal and environmental roles.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Ornamental Plants</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Ornamental plants are cultivated primarily for display and decoration in gardens, homes, parks and public spaces because of their attractive flowers, leaves, or overall form, rather than for direct consumption as food.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Economic Importance</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Ornamental plants generate income through nurseries, landscaping businesses, and export of cut flowers; they create employment for growers, florists and landscape designers; and they add value to real estate by improving the appearance of properties.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Aesthetic Importance</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Ornamentals beautify homes, offices, schools, parks and roadsides, improving the visual appeal of the environment and providing a pleasant atmosphere for relaxation and recreation.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Medicinal Importance</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Some ornamental plants, such as aloe vera and certain flowering shrubs, have medicinal properties and are used in herbal remedies for wounds, skin conditions and other ailments.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Environmental Importance</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Ornamental plants help purify the air by absorbing carbon dioxide and releasing oxygen, reduce noise pollution, provide shade and cooling, prevent soil erosion around compounds, and support pollinators such as bees and butterflies.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Ornamental plants matter for four broad reasons: economic (income/jobs), aesthetic (beauty), medicinal (herbal remedies), and environmental (air purification, erosion control, pollinator support).\n</div>\n',
