    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Choosing the right <span class="learn-keyword">setting or location</span> for each type of ornamental plant ensures healthy growth and maximises its decorative effect.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Common Settings for Ornamental Plants</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Suitable Plant Types</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Home gardens</td><td>Flowering plants, shrubs, foliage plants</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Parks</td><td>Trees, lawn grasses, flowering beds</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Schools</td><td>Trees for shade, shrubs for hedges, lawn grasses</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Offices</td><td>Foliage plants (indoor), flowering plants (outdoor beds)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Roadsides/avenues</td><td>Trees, shrubs as median hedges</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Factors to Consider When Locating Ornamental Plants</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Key factors include the amount of sunlight the site receives (full sun vs shade-tolerant species), available space (trees need more room than lawn grasses), soil type and drainage, purpose (privacy hedge vs decorative bed vs shade), and maintenance access (ease of watering, pruning, mowing).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Matching Plant Type to Setting</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Flowering plants</strong> are best located where they receive adequate sunlight and can be viewed easily, such as garden beds near walkways. <strong>Foliage plants</strong> often tolerate shade and are ideal for indoor offices and shaded corners. <strong>Shrubs</strong> are placed along boundaries for hedges or screens. <strong>Lawn grasses</strong> need open, sunny spaces such as parks and playgrounds. <strong>Trees</strong> require wide, open spaces such as avenues and large compounds. <strong>Climbers</strong> need vertical supports like fences, trellises, and arches.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> WAEC may ask you to match a plant type to its most suitable setting — always link the plant\'s growth requirements (light, space, support) to the features of the setting.\n</div>\n',
