    topicCode: 'SS2-AGR-12',
    module: 'Crop Protection',
    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A <span class="learn-keyword">crop pest</span> is any organism that damages crops, reduces their yield or quality, or otherwise interferes with agricultural production.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Definition of Crop Pests</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Crop pests are organisms — insects, birds, rodents, and larger mammals — that feed on, damage, or otherwise harm growing or stored crops, causing economic loss to farmers.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Examples of Crop Pests</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Typical Damage</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Insects</td><td>Grasshoppers, weevils, aphids, stem borers</td><td>Chewing leaves, boring stems, sucking sap</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Birds</td><td>Quelea birds, weaver birds</td><td>Eating grain, especially rice and sorghum</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rodents</td><td>Rats, mice</td><td>Gnawing stored grain and tubers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Monkeys</td><td>Monkeys, baboons</td><td>Raiding and destroying fruit and maize farms</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Economic Importance (Damage) of Pests</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Pests reduce crop yield and quality, cause post-harvest losses in storage, increase production costs due to control measures, and in severe outbreaks (e.g., locust swarms) can wipe out entire harvests, threatening food security.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Preventive and Control Measures</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Control strategies include cultural methods (crop rotation, early planting, field sanitation, scaring devices for birds), mechanical methods (hand-picking, traps, barriers/fencing against rodents and monkeys), biological control (using natural predators or parasites of the pest), and chemical control (appropriate, judicious use of pesticides/insecticides).</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish a "pest" (an organism that damages the crop, e.g., an insect) from a "disease" (an abnormal condition, often caused by a pathogen). Some pests, like aphids and whiteflies, also spread diseases as vectors — a favourite WAEC link question.\n</div>\n',
