    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  The <span class="learn-keyword">factors of production</span> are the basic resources — land, labour, capital, and entrepreneurship — combined to produce agricultural goods and services.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Land</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Land refers to all natural resources used in production — soil, water, minerals, climate, and space. Its characteristics include fixed supply (cannot be increased overall), immobility (cannot be physically moved from place to place), and variation in quality/fertility. Its reward is <strong>rent</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Labour</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Labour is the human effort — physical and mental — applied to production. It includes skilled labour (e.g., agricultural extension officers) and unskilled labour (e.g., farm hands). Its characteristics include being perishable (a day\'s unused labour cannot be stored) and varying in efficiency. Its reward is <strong>wages</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Capital</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Capital refers to man-made resources used in production — tools, machinery, buildings, and money invested in the farm business. It is created through savings and investment, and is used to boost the productivity of land and labour. Its reward is <strong>interest</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Entrepreneurship</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Entrepreneurship is the organisational and risk-bearing factor — the farmer/manager who combines land, labour and capital, makes key decisions, and bears the risk of loss or gain in the enterprise. Its reward is <strong>profit</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Roles in Agriculture</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Role in Agriculture</th><th>Reward</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Land</td><td>Provides space, soil and natural resources for farming</td><td>Rent</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Labour</td><td>Performs farm operations (planting, weeding, harvesting)</td><td>Wages</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Capital</td><td>Provides tools, machinery, and funds for inputs</td><td>Interest</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Entrepreneurship</td><td>Organises the other factors and bears business risk</td><td>Profit</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Memorise the reward for each factor: Land–Rent, Labour–Wages, Capital–Interest, Entrepreneurship–Profit. WAEC frequently asks students to match factors to their rewards.\n</div>\n',
