    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A <span class="learn-keyword">farm manager</span> is the person responsible for organising and directing all farm resources and operations to achieve the farm\'s production and profit objectives.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Planning</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The farm manager sets clear production goals, decides what enterprises to undertake, and prepares budgets and schedules for farm operations across the season/year.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Organising</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The manager arranges and coordinates resources — land, labour, capital and materials — assigning tasks and responsibilities to workers and ensuring resources are available when and where needed.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Staffing/Directing</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">This involves recruiting, training and supervising farm workers, assigning duties suited to their skills, and motivating staff to achieve production targets efficiently.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Controlling</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The manager monitors ongoing farm operations against the plan, checking that inputs are used efficiently, quality standards are met, and taking corrective action when performance deviates from targets.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Coordinating</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The manager ensures different farm activities (planting, feeding, marketing) work together smoothly and are not in conflict, harmonising the efforts of workers and departments.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">6. Marketing and Record Keeping</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The manager decides how and when to sell produce for the best returns, and maintains accurate records of income, expenditure, production and inventory to evaluate performance and support future planning and loan applications.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">7. Risk and Decision Making</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The manager makes key decisions under uncertainty (weather, price fluctuations, pest outbreaks) and bears responsibility for the consequences, taking measures such as insurance or diversification to manage risk.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The core management functions on a farm are Planning, Organising, Staffing/Directing, Controlling, and Coordinating (often remembered together with marketing and record keeping) — all aimed at efficient, profitable, and sustainable farm operations.\n</div>\n',
